For each word below, write ONE short sentence (12 to 22 words) that uses the word itself, spelled in full, in the sense given. Give it voice and mood: a question, someone speaking, a sigh, delight, a warning. No definitions; show the word in a moment of life. Answer as one JSON object mapping each WORD (as given, upper case) to its sentence. JSON only.

GRID: a pattern of regularly spaced horizontal and vertical lines.
GROUND: the solid part of the earth's surface.
GROUP: any number of entities (members) considered as a unit.
GROWTH: (biology) the process of an individual organism growing organically.
GUARD: a person who keeps watch over something or someone.
HAND: the (prehensile) extremity of the superior limb.
